WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.375
Plotting rewards neat people.

2
00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:04.825
That isn’t a matter of taste.

3
00:00:05.075 --> 00:00:06.900
It’s arithmetic.

4
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.025
Keep your pencil sharp.

5
00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:16.425
On this chart, a fat pencil line can hide a tenth of a mile, and the answer choices are a tenth of a mile apart.

6
00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:20.500
Label every line and every position as you draw it.

7
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.750
In a five-part problem, you’ll need to find your earlier work.

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.700
Work in true, and convert to magnetic or compass only at the end.

9
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:34.250
Give your answers to the nearest degree, and the nearest tenth of a mile.

10
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.400
And if your answer isn’t one of the choices?

11
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.750
Don’t pick the closest one.

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.800
What do you do instead?

13
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.625
Go back and find the step that went wrong.

14
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:49.325
The right answer is almost always there exactly.

15
00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:51.400
That’s lesson one.

16
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.850
Read the rose on the side you’re traveling toward.

17
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.175
Measure on the side scale, level with your work.

18
00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.625
Next time: positions.
